speechtext:
Madam Speaker, my question is directed to the minister responsible for the Treasury Board. Earlier in this question period the hon. member for Prince Edward-Hastings brought up the issue of appointments to the Department of Transport. I read from an ad for foreign service secretaries which was in the Ottawa area on the weekend. The first sentence of the ad reads as follows: "If you are a resident of the province of Quebec or Ontario with secretarial experience and have the ability to take dictation", you may want to work in a foreign embassy.
Could the minister explain to me why Canadian secretaries, to be entitled to work in our foreign missions, should be from the province of Ontario or Quebec?
[Translation}
